# plan.env: the placement plan results/margin.md declares, read by plan.sh (build.sh, verify.sh,
# run.sh) and report.mjs. Written before any binary was built or measured; pack.sh checks that
# margin.md states the same and that the sizes are pads.mjs's.
#   K         placements per comparison
#   R         recorded pairs per placement, after one unrecorded pair
#   PADS_P    the pad of side A's placement i (bytes): base's A side in the A/A comparisons, and
#             in the change comparisons the pad of both base and head (base pad p_i against head
#             pad p_i)
#   PADS_Q    the pad of base's B side in the A/A comparisons (base pad p_i against base pad q_i)
#   DIAG_K    placements of the unpadded diagnostic: base unpadded against base pad p_i, i <= DIAG_K
#   DIAG_R    its recorded pairs per placement
#   STEP      seconds the workload `old` moves a start's monotonic clock on, once its answer is kept
#   OLD_LOW, OLD_HIGH      the Age a start of the workload `old` must send, before and after its turn
#   YOUNG_LOW, YOUNG_HIGH  the same for the workload `young`, whose clock is not moved
# A pad of n bytes is one never-called function of n bytes linked first in .text (build.sh), so
# every function after it moves by n and keeps its order.
K=30
R=8
PADS_P="320 15120 25824 40624 10304 21008 35808 5552 20288 30992 736 15536 26176 36880 10720 21424 36160 5904 16608 31408 1088 15888 26592 37296 11072 21776 36576 6320 16960 31760"
PADS_Q="22848 12160 38336 27648 12880 2192 32464 17680 7008 33184 22496 11808 38000 27312 12528 1840 32064 17280 6592 32768 22096 11408 37584 26896 16224 1440 31712 16928 6256 36528"
DIAG_K=8
DIAG_R=8
STEP=10005
OLD_LOW=10005
OLD_HIGH=10020
YOUNG_LOW=0
YOUNG_HIGH=15
